<title>USA: Air Products files $300 mln debt shelf.</title>
<headline>Air Products files $300 mln debt shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air Products and Chemicals Inc filed Monday with the Securities and Exchange Commission a shelf registration to sell up to $300 million in medium-term notes, series G.</p>
<p>The offering will be made through Lehman Brothers and Goldman, Sachs &amp; Co.</p>
<p>Net proceeds will be used for general corporate purposes which may include the refunding of maturing debt and the repurchase of the company's common stock and acquisitions.</p>
<p>The company is based in Allentown, Pa.</p>
</text>
